    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on exploiting favorable matchups, anchored by the elite 72.06 projection of **Kyle Tucker** and the 70.90 efficiency of **Drake Baldwin**. **Kyle Tucker** remains our most reliable asset against King, where the lack of an elite holding threat allows him to operate with aggressive intent, while **Drake Baldwin** benefits from a massive 5.64 xERA matchup against Williamson, positioning him as the cornerstone of our daily production. Both **Tommy White** and **Henry Bolte** offer high upside at 62.71 and 65.40 respectively, as they draw Kikuchi in what project to be high-run-environment conditions with wind and park factors providing double-digit boosts to their base outlooks.\n\nWhile the core is strong, we must navigate the significant risks posed by the rainouts of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Gunnar Henderson**, which drastically shorten our bench depth. Our most difficult decision centered on **Wade Meckler**, who finished just outside the starting rotation with a 44.60 score. While **Wade Meckler** benefits from favorable park factors, the optimizer preferred the superior run-production outlook of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Josh Jung**, whose middle-of-the-order slots provide a higher ceiling for RBI in tighter contests against Rasmussen and Manaea. \n\nCaution is advised regarding the bottom of our lineup, as **Nasim Nunez** and **Brayan Rocchio** carry sub-50 efficiency scores, primarily suppressed by their #9 batting order spots and the high-skill profiles of opposing arms like Anderson and Tolle. We are prioritizing speed and high-OBP potential today, keeping a close eye on the late-inning leverage of **Jackson Merrill**, whose 58.14 score is buoyed by a slow opposing pitcher delivery\u2014a key variable for our aggressive stolen base mandate. We will be monitoring the progress of **Heliot Ramos** and **Liam Hicks** closely, as their platoon-adjusted projections suggest they are the most susceptible to being pulled if their early-game at-bats against tough arms fail to generate traffic.",
